  "_comment": "Spoken-media registry for scripts/fetch_podcast_signal.py (the Aradio source lane). Every source is read through tuber-api, never directly, and read-only (no summarize/generation endpoints). kind=channel -> GET /api/channel/{channel_id} (the channel's long-form uploads; live-streamed videos are NOT listed there: verified 2026-10-30, OpenAI's DevDay 2026 keynote stream and four livestreamed Cognitive Revolution episodes were absent from that listing even when paged back past their air dates, so channels that publish by livestream also carry a channel-constrained search entry). kind=search -> GET /api/search?q=..., keeping ONLY results whose channelId equals channel_id: this is how first-party live streams such as earnings calls are found, and the channel constraint is mandatory so third-party re-streams can never enter. kind=podcast -> GET /api/podcast/episodes?rss=... (metadata and ~80-word show notes; tuber does not transcribe RSS audio). Video transcripts come from GET /api/video/{id}/transcript. ai_filter=true marks a mixed-topic show: an episode is kept only when its title/description passes the AI-topicality check. min_duration_s drops clips. Every full-episode podcast surveyed on 2026-10-30 is on YouTube; channel IDs below were verified live through tuber that day (several obvious handles are clips-only or dormant, so use these IDs, not handles).",
